A||||18||Rodney||A letter about the Fiero Stores actions?||||1||
Z||000000||Rodney||09-28-2001||08:35 PM||||I am considering drafting and including a letter detailing the fact that the Fiero Store has copied one of my original designs and is looking to copy more in the future. I would like it to be in good taste. Anyone a good writer that can help? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||kempo||09-28-2001||08:48 PM||||I will revise it for you to perfection! Honestly, I think you should go for legal action against them.  Keep us posted.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/kempsig.jpg"> <BR>87 Fiero GT / 5 Speed<BR>86 Fiero 2m4 - FOR SALE||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero5||09-28-2001||08:54 PM||||I wonder if there is a way to get all our names on that document? Sort of like a petition.<P>Just a thought.<P>Steve||||reg||5
Z||000003||Oreif||09-28-2001||10:27 PM||||OK everyone, You can highlight the below and Email it to The Fiero Store. If you feel it requires some "massaging" feel free to do so. I typed this as a general "form" letter.<BR>You may use it as you need to in order to get your point across. Mine will be mailed tonight when I get home.<P>Update: Email Sent!<BR>___________________________________<P>To: The Fiero Store<BR>From: A Concerned Fiero Owner<P>Smitty at the Fiero Store,<P>It has come to the attention of myself and many others in the Fiero Community that you have copied a design from Rodney Dickman. The Select Arm Rebuild Kit was originally designed and sold by him.<BR>In an Email posted on Pennock’s Fiero Forum, You have openly admitted using his design and further insulted the Fiero Community by stating you would copy other designs of his you deemed popular. The Fiero market is not that large. Many Fiero Enthusiasts support the community by designing and selling items that are improved or obsolete so we can all benefit from it. The posted Email has met with a very negative response towards your business. You can see the responses yourself at this link: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010599.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010599.html</A> <P>As you can see by the responses, it looks like the Rebuild kit you are selling is going to cause some customers to have second thoughts about purchasing items from you and I would guess that particular product will have low sales. I feel that this kind of bad press may also cause some people to be shy about designing and marketing other obsolete items for fear that you would just copy their design and undercut them on the price.  Many people like Rodney spend many hours designing alternative parts to maintain our aging cars. It is demeaning to have your hours of design work stolen from you so another business can profit from it. This act makes it seem you are more interested in profits/sales than supporting the Fiero Community. With the popularity of the Fiero Community utilizing the Internet for problem solving, troubleshooting, and acquiring hard to find parts, This type of bad business practices can spread quickly and damage the business’s reputation very quickly. Your business has done a fine job of supporting the Fiero Community over the years, But this latest endeavor has given your reputation a “Black eye”.<BR>I sincerely hope that you can find a way to correct this and restore your reputation. <P>Thank You,<P> <P><BR>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B></FONT><P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||09-28-2001||10:52 PM||||Go get 'em Rodney!  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>I'm not so well versed...only opinions here.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||IwannaIRM||09-28-2001||11:33 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> Ditto...what Oreif said.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>------------------<BR>AIM - SWags2933<P>84 Fiero SE (being modified)<BR>88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000006||Back On Holiday||09-28-2001||11:36 PM||||WELL SAID!<P>I know I myself will make the Fiero Store my LAST Resort to purchase from if at all.  if it costs twice as much somewhere else, then so be it.  I have bought items from Rodney, and although I missed catching him at Carlisle to thank him for the v6 steel tubes, the headlight rebuild kits, and other various things I have bought from him, I will continue to look at his site first for what I am after.<BR>I find the Fiero Stores prices kinda high anyway on most items you can get somewhere else, without getting into specifics...I know I've saved a few hundred bucks by shopping around.<P>anyway, I believe the select arm rebuild kit is $12.50, whats the FS going to sell it for, $12.49?  whats it cost Rodney to make it, $8,$10? whatever it is, the guys gotta make a profit...sorry I'm just letting out some steam.<P><P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||6
