Z||000010||Back On Holiday||09-29-2001||03:17 AM||||1 More....My car has something to say about the Fiero Store...<BR>(I hope nobody gets mad at me for these pics)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero2_1.JPG"> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000011||Raydar||09-29-2001||01:34 PM||||Composed my own...<P>----- Original Message ----- <BR>From: Steve <BR>To: info@fierostore.com <BR>Sent: Saturday, September 29, 2001 1:30 PM<BR>Subject: Select Arm Rebuild Kits<P><BR>I have been a customer or the Fiero Store for several years. <P>However...<BR>Since you feel the need to steal the design of another, I feel the need to take my business elsewhere.<P>BTW... This story is now widespread on many Fiero mailing lists and bulletin boards.<BR>Let's see how many other people voice their displeasure by making you their *last* choice.<P>Steve Hamilton<BR>---------------<P>Back On Holiday, LOL!!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000012||chester||09-29-2001||02:07 PM||||The Fiero Store responded with this.<P>To Rodney Dickman and The Fiero Community:<P>The Fiero Store would like to extend its sincerest apologies to Rodney<BR>Dickman for producing an unauthorized copy of his select arm rebuild kits.<BR>After receiving a number of calls from our customers asking us to offer some<BR>of Rodney's parts, we immediately contacted Mr. Dickman. We were hoping to<BR>use a supplier from within the Fiero community with a good reputation for<BR>quality parts. Unfortunately, Mr. Dickman made it quite clear, in no<BR>uncertain terms, that he did not want to do business with The Fiero Store.<BR>As a result, we were forced to manufacture the select arm rebuild kits<BR>ourselves in order to bring our customers the part they demanded.<BR>Regretfully, we were irresponsible in designing a part that was identical to<BR>Mr. Dickman's select arm rebuild kit. There was never any malice intended<BR>toward Mr. Dickman or his business. We have and will continue to recommend<BR>RodneyDickman.com to all of our customers who need parts that we do not<BR>offer. As a gesture of good faith, we will also send Mr. Dickman our entire<BR>inventory of select arm rebuild kits. The Fiero Store will no longer carry<BR>this part and will direct all of our customers looking for that part to Mr.<BR>Dickman.<P>We would also like to sincerely apologize to our customers and to the Fiero<BR>community at large for inadvertently abusing their trust. Our only intention<BR>in carrying the select arm rebuild kits was to give our customers the part<BR>they asked for. Had we viewed Rodney Dickman as a "competitor," rather than<BR>an ally, we certainly would not have asked him to supply us with parts nor<BR>would we recommend him to so many of our customers. We have a lot of respect<BR>for Rodney and all of the hard work he has done to help Fiero owners.<P>In the coming months and years, you will see many new products coming from<BR>The Fiero Store. Many of our new parts will not be found anywhere else in<BR>the world. Some of those new products may be similar to parts offered by<BR>Rodney Dickman. In order for a company to grow, it must provide its<BR>customers with the products and service that they demand, regardless of who<BR>else may offer a similar product or service. However, the Fiero community<BR>can rest assured that none of our new products will be exactly the same as<BR>Rodney's. We will take great care in making sure that our products offer<BR>unique value separate and apart from anything offered by Mr. Dickman.<P>We hope that Mr. Dickman and the rest of the Fiero community will accept our<BR>apology. We made a mistake, have taken steps to correct that mistake, and<BR>will take full responsibility for our actions. We look forward to continuing<BR>to serve Fiero owners around the world to the best of our ability and we<BR>thank all of our customers for their continued support.<P>Sincerely,<BR>Smitty<BR>President<BR>The Fiero Store<BR>----- Original Message -----<BR>From: Rob D &lt;rob.renee@verizon.net&gt;<BR>To: &lt;info@fierostore.com&gt;<BR>Sent: Saturday, September 29, 2001 8:23 AM<BR>Subject: Rodney Dickmans Design<P><BR>&gt; Hi,<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; Just wanted to express my disgust with your blatant dishonor for someone<BR>&gt; else's research and ideas.  You stole an idea from a well known Fiero<BR>&gt; enthusiast and blatantly told him that you will continue to do so if you<BR>see<BR>&gt; the prospect of making $$$.  Just wanted to let you know that you will<BR>LOOSE<BR>&gt; more money by the business that will stray from your door.  A lot of us<BR>&gt; Fiero owners have morals.  With that said I WILL NOT PURCHASE ANOTHER<BR>&gt; ACCESSORY FROM YOU UNTIL YOU DROP THE PRODUCT AND GIVE RODNEY DICKMAN A<BR>&gt; FORMAL APOLOGY! There are many of us that feel the same way.  Enclosed are<BR>&gt; some of the emails floating on the lists about what has happened and other<BR>&gt; points of view. You might want to read them so you can see what was<BR>started<BR>&gt; by this forgery. Might want to read the attachments.  These are just a<BR>few.<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; Regards,<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; Robert and Renee Dabrowski, former customers Fiero Store.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroFanaticus2||09-29-2001||02:14 PM||||Yep, I got that letter too --- to all 3 of the different email addresses I sent them nasty letters from.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I'm glad to see they have done something about it though, but I am still disgusted.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||09-29-2001||02:24 PM||||Yup, I got it too. (Detailed in another post)<P>Rodney,<P>Please keep us posted, if there's anything new.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Rodney||09-29-2001||02:47 PM||||Fiero owners:<P>I will be drafting a letter asking all the Fiero<BR>websites with a link to the Fiero Store to consider<BR>removing their website link. I will collect all the<BR>information that has been passed on to me lately and<BR>ask them to make a choice as to weather they would like<BR>to keep their website link on their page or remove it<BR>considering the poor business ethics they have<BR>demonstrated. I will work with an attorney and I also<BR>have a friend who is a professor of criminal law at a<BR>major university to draft this correspondence. The<BR>email I received below makes me want to do this all the<BR>more.<P><BR>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P><BR>Hello Listees, This whole Fiero store thing just got a<BR>little worse. I just got a new catalog from a Fiero<BR>parts vendor in Ohio. His name is Nolan Bishop. For<BR>those who do not now him, He is the person who offers<BR>chrome parts to replace just about anything on a Fiero.<BR>Nolan also builds a mandrel bent cold air intake for<BR>the Fiero. He was supplying them for the Fiero store<BR>for a while, until they informed him that it was not a<BR>high volume mover so they were now going to discontinue<BR>them. Then in August, Nolan received a new Fiero store<BR>catalog. In the new catalog was a copy of the Intake<BR>tube assembly that Nolan developed being featured as<BR>"Their New Product" (copied like Rodney's parts). I<BR>have spent my fair share of money at the Fiero Store in<BR>the past, But in support of my fellow Fiero people,<BR>There will never be another parts order from us to the<BR>Fiero Store.<P>Darrell Morse (Member of Minnesota Fieros Forever)<BR>21411 Concord ST. NW.<BR>Elk River, MN. 55330<BR>(763) 441-5679<BR>"Custom Fiero Machine work"<BR>Bored out V6 Throttle Body's and Plenums (from 52MM to<BR>57MM<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||fierobaby||09-29-2001||03:05 PM||||just wrote the fiero store a letter knowing the lost some good customers and not to expect me ever again!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Back On Holiday||09-29-2001||03:16 PM||||To TFS- THATS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"><P>The only Reason why they did that is to save face, and try and get some business back.  They(TFS) know that we all turned on them and this was the ONLY way to back out...carefully.  They did it to Nolan?<P>UNCALLED FOR.  I'm still going to make them last, cause - Once a BACK Stabber, Always a BACK Stabber.<P>Anybody know if theres a site I may have missed with a parts Database similar to 'The Big Fiero Parts Book'?  I envision a site database with price comparison, links to that site, quality reports and so forth.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000018||Jaygee79||09-29-2001||03:29 PM||||Hey, I sent that email to them and this is what I got back:<P><BR>To Rodney Dickman and The Fiero Community:<BR> <BR>The Fiero Store would like to extend its sincerest apologies to Rodney<BR>Dickman for producing an unauthorized copy of his select arm rebuild kits.<BR>After receiving a number of calls from our customers asking us to offer some<BR>of Rodney's parts, we immediately contacted Mr. Dickman. We were hoping to<BR>use a supplier from within the Fiero community with a good reputation for<BR>quality parts. Unfortunately, Mr. Dickman made it quite clear, in no<BR>uncertain terms, that he did not want to do business with The Fiero Store.<BR>As a result, we were forced to manufacture the select arm rebuild kits<BR>ourselves in order to bring our customers the part they demanded.<BR>Regretfully, we were irresponsible in designing a part that was identical to<BR>Mr. Dickman's select arm rebuild kit. There was never any malice intended<BR>toward Mr. Dickman or his business. We have and will continue to recommend<BR>RodneyDickman.com to all of our customers who need parts that we do not<BR>offer. As a gesture of good faith, we will also send Mr. Dickman our entire<BR>inventory of select arm rebuild kits. The Fiero Store will no longer carry<BR>this part and will direct all of our customers looking for that part to Mr.<BR>Dickman.<BR> <BR>We would also like to sincerely apologize to our customers and to the Fiero<BR>community at large for inadvertently abusing their trust. Our only intention<BR>in carrying the select arm rebuild kits was to give our customers the part<BR>they asked for. Had we viewed Rodney Dickman as a "competitor," rather than<BR>an ally, we certainly would not have asked him to supply us with parts nor<BR>would we recommend him to so many of our customers. We have a lot of respect<BR>for Rodney and all of the hard work he has done to help Fiero owners.<BR> <BR>In the coming months and years, you will see many new products coming from<BR>The Fiero Store. Many of our new parts will not be found anywhere else in<BR>the world. Some of those new products may be similar to parts offered by<BR>Rodney Dickman. In order for a company to grow, it must provide its<BR>customers with the products and service that they demand, regardless of who<BR>else may offer a similar product or service. However, the Fiero community<BR>can rest assured that none of our new products will be exactly the same as<BR>Rodney's. We will take great care in making sure that our products offer<BR>unique value separate and apart from anything offered by Mr. Dickman.<BR> <BR>We hope that Mr. Dickman and the rest of the Fiero community will accept our<BR>apology. We made a mistake, have taken steps to correct that mistake, and<BR>will take full responsibility for our actions. We look forward to continuing<BR>to serve Fiero owners around the world to the best of our ability and we<BR>thank all of our customers for their continued support.<BR> <BR>Sincerely,<BR>Smitty<BR>President<BR>The Fiero Store<BR>||||reg||1
